---
import InstallButton from "./InstallButton.astro";

interface Props {
  version: string;
}

const { version } = Astro.props;

const userscriptHref = `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/deckmasterbeam/SniffiesProjects/userscript-${version}/dist/sniffies-tools.user.js`;
const chromeHref = `https://github.com/deckmasterbeam/SniffiesProjects/releases/download/chrome-${version}/sniffies-chrome.zip`;
---

<h2>Installation</h2>

<p>There are two builds: a userscript and a Chrome extension.</p>
<p>
  There are three three ways to install these builds based on your use case:
</p>

<h3>iOS (Safari)</h3>

<p>Install via the Userscripts app:</p>

<ol>
  <li>
    Install the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/userscripts/id1463298887"
      >Userscripts</a
    > app
  </li>
  <li>Enable it in <strong>Settings → Safari → Extensions</strong></li>
  <li>
    Tap the install button below to go to the userscript page. On that page, tap
    the button next to the URL (highlighted in red in the screenshot below),
    then tap the userscript extension. Userscripts will detect the script and
    prompt you to install it. Tap <strong>Install</strong> (it'll say <strong
      >Update</strong
    > instead if you're reinstalling a newer version).
  </li>
</ol>

<figure>
  <img
    src="/images/sniffies-userscript-install-1.PNG"
    alt="The website settings button in Safari's address bar that opens the extensions menu"
  />
  <figcaption>
    Tap this button in the address bar to access Manage Extensions. In that
    menu, tap the userscript extension.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<figure>
  <img
    src="/images/sniffies-userscript-install-2.PNG"
    alt="Userscripts extension prompting the user that a userscript has been detected and offering to install it"
  />
  <figcaption>
    Userscripts will detect the script and prompt you to install (or update) it
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<InstallButton
  href={userscriptHref}
  label={`Install iOS Userscript v${version}`}
/>

<p>
  <strong>Updating:</strong> come back to this page and tap the install button again
  whenever a new version is released — Userscripts will show
  <strong>Update</strong> instead of <strong>Install</strong>.
</p>

<h3>Desktop (Chrome Extension)</h3>

<p>The extension isn't on the Chrome Web Store, so installation is manual:</p>

<ol>
  <li>Download the zip below and unzip it</li>
  <li>
    Go to <code>chrome://extensions</code> and enable <strong
      >Developer mode</strong
    > (top right)
  </li>
  <li>Click <strong>Load unpacked</strong> and select the unzipped folder</li>
</ol>

<InstallButton
  href={chromeHref}
  label={`Download Chrome Extension v${version}`}
/>

<p>
  <strong>Updating:</strong> download the new zip and unzip it over the same folder,
  then go back to <code>chrome://extensions</code> and click the reload icon on the
  Sniffies extension's card. If you unzipped to a new folder instead, remove the old
  extension first and <strong>Load unpacked</strong> the new folder.
</p>

<h3>Desktop (Tampermonkey)</h3>

<p>
  If you'd rather run the userscript build on desktop instead of the Chrome
  extension, install it via <a href="https://www.tampermonkey.net/"
    >Tampermonkey</a
  >:
</p>

<ol>
  <li>
    Install the <a href="https://www.tampermonkey.net/">Tampermonkey</a> extension
    from the Chrome Web Store
  </li>
  <li>
    Click the install button below. Tampermonkey will detect the script and
    prompt you to install it. Click <strong>Install</strong> (it'll say
    <strong>Update</strong> instead if you're reinstalling a newer version).
  </li>
</ol>

<InstallButton
  href={userscriptHref}
  label={`Install Tampermonkey Userscript v${version}`}
/>

<p>
  <strong>Updating:</strong> come back to this page and click the install button again
  whenever a new version is released — Tampermonkey will show
  <strong>Update</strong> instead of <strong>Install</strong>.
</p>
